From: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] b43: program the PAPD epsilon offset on radio 2057 rev 8

b43_phy_initn() writes nphy->papd_epsilon_offset[] into the EPS table
adjust registers, but nothing ever computes it, so the PAPD engine gets an
offset of zero.

brcmsmac computes it at the end of its PAPD calibration:

	offset = -60 + 27 + eps_offset - (padgain_delta[pad_gain] + 1) / 2

with eps_offset -1 for this radio in 2 GHz, and pad_gain the index its PAPD
gain search settles on. b43 has no PAPD calibration, so take the index the
vendor driver settles on: an MMIO capture of wl 6.30.102.7 on a BCM6362
shows 15 for both cores, and the -24 that comes out of the formula is what
it writes. b43 currently writes 0, which is 24 dB off.

The pad gain delta table is the one the previous patches already carry, so
the formula is evaluated rather than its result hardcoded: when the gain
search arrives, only the index has to come from it.




Verified: records #286-#288, from "PHY.MOD  addr=0x0298 val=0xf400 mask=0xff80"
Verified: records #13842-#13847, from "PHY.MOD  addr=0x0298 val=0xf400 mask=0xff80"
Link: https://github.com/aleferri/b43-6362-wip/blob/e916c8a/router-data/dsl-3580l/opinit-ch1-ch6-bw20.decoded

Signed-off-by: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.h
@@ -835,6 +835,11 @@
 #define B43_NPHY_RADAR_T2_MIN			B43_PHY_N(0x295)
 #define B43_NPHY_TXPWRCTRLDAMPING		B43_PHY_N(0x296)
 #define B43_NPHY_PAPD_EN0			B43_PHY_N(0x297) /* PAPD Enable0 TBD */
+/* Pad gain index the PAPD gain search settles on, from a capture of the vendor
+ * driver on radio 2057 rev 8 in 2.4 GHz. Placeholder for the search itself.
+ */
+#define B43_NPHY_PAPD_CAL_PAD_GAIN		15
+
 #define B43_NPHY_EPS_TABLE_ADJ0			B43_PHY_N(0x298) /* EPS Table Adj0 TBD */
 #define B43_NPHY_EPS_OVERRIDEI_0		B43_PHY_N(0x299)
 #define B43_NPHY_EPS_OVERRIDEQ_0		B43_PHY_N(0x29A)
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
@@ -6061,6 +6061,40 @@
 	b43_ntab_write_bulk(dev, B43_NTAB32(33, 0), 64, zero);
 }
 
+/* The offset the PAPD engine applies to the epsilon table. brcmsmac computes it
+ * at the end of its PAPD calibration as
+ *
+ *	offset = -60 + 27 + eps_offset - (padgain_delta[pad_gain] + 1) / 2
+ *
+ * where eps_offset is -1 for this radio in 2 GHz and pad_gain is the index the
+ * PAPD gain search settles on. b43 has no PAPD calibration, so the offset stays
+ * at zero and the engine runs 24 dB off.
+ *
+ * Until the calibration is there, use the index the vendor driver settles on,
+ * which an MMIO capture on a BCM6362 shows to be 15 for both cores: the offset
+ * that comes out, -24, is what it programs.
+ */
+static void b43_nphy_papd_epsilon_offset(struct b43_wldev *dev)
+{
+	struct b43_phy *phy = &dev->phy;
+	struct b43_phy_n *nphy = phy->n;
+	const s16 *delta;
+	int offset, core;
+
+	if (phy->rev != 8 || phy->radio_rev != 8 ||
+	    b43_current_band(dev->wl) != NL80211_BAND_2GHZ)
+		return;
+
+	delta = b43_ntab_get_rf_pwr_offset_table(dev);
+	if (!delta)
+		return;
+
+	offset = -60 + 27 - 1 - (delta[B43_NPHY_PAPD_CAL_PAD_GAIN] + 1) / 2;
+
+	for (core = 0; core < 2; core++)
+		nphy->papd_epsilon_offset[core] = offset;
+}
+
 static int b43_phy_initn(struct b43_wldev *dev)
 {
 	struct ssb_sprom *sprom = dev->dev->bus_sprom;
@@ -6163,6 +6197,7 @@
 	}
 
 	if (b43_nphy_ipa(dev)) {
+		b43_nphy_papd_epsilon_offset(dev);
 		b43_phy_set(dev, B43_NPHY_PAPD_EN0, 0x1);
 		b43_phy_maskset(dev, B43_NPHY_EPS_TABLE_ADJ0, 0x007F,
 				nphy->papd_epsilon_offset[0] << 7);

Note per il repo, non per la mailing list:

  - Derivazione, tutta verificabile: il vendore scrive 0xf400 con maschera
    0xff80 su 0x298 e 0x29c, cioe' -24 nel campo a 9 bit segnato. Dalla formula
    -34 - (delta[i] + 1) / 2 = -24 segue delta[i] = -21, che nella tabella dei
    valori rev7 (quella di patches/b43/0002) e' l'indice 15.
  - Verifica: harness, flow init -> il port ora scrive 0xf400 su entrambi i
    registri, identico alla cattura. Prima scriveva 0x0000.
  - Cosa NON e': la calibrazione PAPD. Questa e' una costante che viene da una
    cattura su una board, al posto di uno zero che non viene da niente. Quando
    ci sara' la ricerca del gain (docs/papd-cal-map.md punto 3) l'indice arriva
    da lei e la define sparisce.
  - Ordine: dopo 0002, che porta la tabella da cui si indicizza.
  - NON provata su hardware. Questa tocca la predistorsione del PA: e' fra le
    prime da misurare.
